            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for brightness, then the Urdu for scorching heat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: سائرن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سائرن — sāiran — \"a siren\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سائرن سن کر سب باہر آئے۔ sāiran sun kar sab bāhar āe. Hearing the siren, everyone came outside."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سائرن (sāiran) is borrowed from English siren. Fire engines, ambulances and the police all have one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
